				\begin{document}$${p}_{ntmj}^{(i)}$$\end{document}pntmj(i) is evaluated for each sample n, cell type t, CpG site m, and methylation status j = 0, 1; each calculation is independent of the input data dimensions, hence evaluating p(i) is O(NTM). Second, αnt must be evaluated, which involves summing over M sites for each n and t, giving overall complexity O(NTM). Finally, updating βtm requires summing over all cfDNA individuals and the reference cell type data, again giving overall complexity O(NTM). Overall, this means that CelFiE scales linearly in sample size, number of CpGs, and number of cell types.

